@flexiarg test-registry/rerun-when-the-warrant-fails
@title Full Rerun Only When The Warrant Fails Or The Lane Demands It
@keywords full-rerun, lane, pre-push, invariant, first-run, stale-sha, bounded
@audience reviewers, lane-policy authors
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; Joe's ruling 2026-09-14: full rerun mandatory pre-push and on invariant-relevant lanes; test_registry.clj `review` :rerun-required outcome)
@references [test-registry/bind-warrant-to-the-diff test-registry/spot-check-at-the-declared-rate]
@see-also buffer-cleaner/exempt-the-in-use
@why the saving is not unconditional: some situations structurally require execution, just as some buffers are structurally in use. Deciding them by a score would erode them.
@how require the declared namespace command (never the unbounded suite) when any of: no warrant (:unwarranted handoff); the record check refuses (stale manifest, uncovered path, environment mismatch, incomplete chain); the lane is :pre-push or :invariant; the namespace's tests are new or changed since their last warranted run (first run of this test content). Otherwise the lane is routine and the spot-check applies. The lane and the reason are recorded; the rerun is itself registered, so it becomes the next warrant.
@violation-signature an unwarranted handoff spot-checked; an invariant lane on the routine path; a full rerun expanded to the whole suite; a rerun that is not registered, so the next reviewer reruns again; "tests changed" left undeclared so the first-run rule cannot be applied.
! conclusion: Execution is required, per namespace and registered, exactly when the warrant fails or a structural lane demands it; everything else is record check plus spot-check.

  + context: A reviewer must pick a lane for each namespace under review.

  + IF:
    A namespace's warrant is missing, refused, or in a mandatory lane.

  + HOWEVER:
    Most deliveries add or change tests, so the first-run rule applies often and the saving is smaller than "run once" suggests; and unregistered reruns throw the saving away for the next reviewer.

  + THEN:
    Rerun the declared namespace command, register it, record lane and reason; route other namespaces to the routine lane.

  + BECAUSE:
    Structural requirements are not priced away; the registry removes only the duplication that has no reason.

  + evidence: futon2 cb5f8b1288 (WM-03 P10 part 2): tests changed in cascade_model_manifest_test (34→35 deftests) and receipt_construction_test (modified); shadow_cascade_g_test unchanged (3 deftests) but the code under it changed — under this pattern only that one namespace would have been routine; the reviewer reran all three.
